{"p4": {"friction": "Theorem 1.1 is labelled \"Theorem 1.1 (Corollary 5.2)\": a restatement pointer between two results that differ slightly in hypotheses (\"affine\" vs \"FSch^qt\"). No relation type covers restated-as or proved-as cleanly. Also, \"this construction defines a contravariant functor Spec\" (Prop. 4.7) uses the word 'defines' for a proved functoriality.", "doubt": "Claim 6: whether a restatement-pointer counts as equivalent-to. Claim 10: whether dropping the FSch^qt hypothesis from a proves object makes it unfaithful.", "missing_context": "The full proofs and section text. The input has only the abstract, part of the introduction and the result statements, so depends-on could not be checked (none was claimed).", "proposed_change": "Add to proves: 'If the object omits a hypothesis of the result, grade wrong-relation (or not-in-paper); state which.' Add to equivalent-to a near-miss: 'Theorem X (Corollary Y)' labels are pointers, not equivalence claims.", "process_observation": "Claims 2 and 10, and claims 9 and 18, are near-duplicates of the same result from the same extractor. Deduplication before grading would save grader effort."}}
